<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3505" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκρό-ᾱμα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>,
			τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>anything heard</i>, esp. <i>with pleasure, piece read,
				recited, played</i> or <i>sung</i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Smp.</u>
				2.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Hier.</u>
				1.14
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. καὶ ὁράματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>EN</u>
					1173b18
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. καὶ πότοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					31.25.4
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> pl. for
			concrete, <i>lecturers, singers</i>, or <i>players</i>, esp.
			during meals, <i><span class="en">
				Phylarch.
				62
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>BCH</u>
				30.272
			</span></i> (Delph.), <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				4.20.10
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				16.21.12
			</span></i>; soin Lat., <i>acroama</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Cic.
				<u>Sest.</u>
				54.116
			</span></i>, etc.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
